description:
[narrowed from route-edit-430450f8] Edit repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/docs-align-tick.ts. This is ONE contiguous string replacement. Use the exact strings below verbatim; do not re-derive your own anchor. The new code is fully wired on the live path and adds no unreferenced symbol.

old_string (this exact 6-line block, which occurs exactly once in the file):
  const vocabulary = await deriveNamingVocabulary(documents);
  const scan = await resolveDocsAlignScan({
    type: "docs_align_scan",
    corpus: { documents },
    live_truth: { existing_paths, unit_names },
    invariants: ["timelessness", "naming_alignment", "setup_enablement"],

new_string:
  const vocabulary = await deriveNamingVocabulary(documents);
  let advertised_shapes: string[] = [];
  try {
    const base = (process.env["DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT"] ?? "http://127.0.0.1:8100").replace(/\/+$/, "");
    const res = await fetch(`${base}/registry/shapes`, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(10_000) });
    if (res.ok) {
      const j = (await res.json()) as unknown;
      const arr = Array.isArray(j)
        ? j
        : Array.isArray((j as { shapes?: unknown })?.shapes)
          ? (j as { shapes: unknown[] }).shapes
          : [];
      advertised_shapes = arr.filter((s): s is string => typeof s === "string");
    }
  } catch {
    advertised_shapes = [];
  }
  const scan = await resolveDocsAlignScan({
    type: "docs_align_scan",
    corpus: { documents },
    live_truth: { existing_paths, unit_names, advertised_shapes },
    invariants: ["timelessness", "naming_alignment", "setup_enablement", "accuracy"],

Everything after that block — the `vocabulary,` line, `max_findings: 100,` and the closing `});` — stays exactly as it is. Do not touch them. No import is needed: process.env, fetch and AbortSignal are globals here. This has been verified to typecheck cleanly (`bun run typecheck`, no errors) with the patch applied to a copy of the vessel.

WHY IT MUST BE ONE CHANGE: an earlier attempt added a standalone helper and left the wiring for a follow-up. It was correctly rejected — "compose adds top-level function fetchAdvertisedShapes with zero readers, not exported and not wired — a write-only hollow addition". Here the fetch is inlined as a statement whose result is consumed two lines below, so nothing is unreferenced.

WHAT IT FIXES: the `accuracy` invariant in docs-align-scan.ts has never once executed, for two independent reasons this single edit closes together. (1) It was absent from the invariants array passed by this caller. (2) Its branch is gated at docs-align-scan.ts line 236 on `pointer.live_truth.advertised_shapes`, and this caller built live_truth as `{ existing_paths, unit_names }` only — both from the local filesystem, exactly as the comment above says: "Assemble live_truth from local filesystem only". The tick never queried the discovery registry, so advertised_shapes was permanently undefined and the branch was skipped even when requested. accuracy is the only invariant that compares a document against live truth; the other three check style, vocabulary and file existence.

WHY IT IS SAFE TO ENABLE NOW: enabling accuracy was previously unsafe because its proximity guard produced false positives — on docs/shapes/README.md it flagged the field names `columns` and `sample` in the sentence "columns, and sample where the shape is tabular". That guard was tightened at docs-align-scan.ts line 248 (`(?:\w+\s+)*shape` became `shapes?\b`, requiring adjacency) and the acceptance test now passes: docs_align_scan with invariants ["accuracy"] and all 385 live advertised shapes over five shape-heavy documents returns ZERO findings.

Every failure path leaves advertised_shapes as an empty array — non-ok response, JSON parse failure, unreachable discovery, timeout — and with an empty array the accuracy branch finds nothing, which is exactly today's behaviour. The change can improve the result or no-op; it cannot throw.

Do NOT modify walkMd, walkScripts, deriveNamingVocabulary, or any other function in this file.

